{
    "article_summary": "The article describes a transition-metal-free photocatalytic S-N coupling reaction between sodium organosulfinates and hydroxamic acids to synthesize acylsulfonamides. Using 4CzBN as a photocatalyst and Na2S2O4 as a reductant, the method operates via an energy transfer process to generate singlet oxygen, which facilitates the formation of a nitrosocarbonyl intermediate. The reaction demonstrates broad substrate scope, including aryl and alkyl sulfinates as well as various hydroxamic acids and N-hydroxycarbamates.",
